  "notes": "Five identical inverting op-amp stages drawn on a ~12 deg tilt; every op-amp has its '-' mark on the UPPER input pin (the one next to the triangle's top vertex) and its '+' mark on the LOWER pin, and every stage puts its feedback element (a capacitor or an inductor) from the output back to that upper '-' pin. Net map: 0 = all six GND symbols (15,16,17,18,21,23) plus everything they touch: GND 21 -> in+ of Op-Amp 0, GND 16 -> in+ of Op-Amp 12, GND 15 -> in+ of Op-Amp 7, GND 23 -> in+ of Op-Amp 4, GND 18 -> bottom lead of V-DC 2, GND 17 -> bottom lead of I-DC 14. n1 = in- of Op-Amp 0 = top lead of V-DC 2 = left plate of Capacitor 20 (T-junction at (230,65) where the feedback wire drops onto the V-DC diagonal). n2 = out of Op-Amp 0 = right plate of Capacitor 20 = left lead of Resistor 11. n3 = in- of Op-Amp 1 = right lead of Resistor 11 = left lead of Inductor 13 (three-way join at (346,144), confirmed by pixel dump). n4 = out of Op-Amp 1 = right lead of Inductor 13 = left lead of Resistor 3. n5 = the long right-hand rail: right lead of Resistor 3 runs from (506,247) straight down-left to (362,470), picking up the right lead of Resistor 5 at the T at (426,372) and ending at the right lead of Resistor 8. n6 = in- of Op-Amp 12 = top lead of I-DC 14 = left lead of Inductor 9. n7 = out of Op-Amp 12 = right lead of Inductor 9 = left lead of Resistor 6. n8 = in- of Op-Amp 7 = right lead of Resistor 6 = left plate of Capacitor 19. n9 = out of Op-Amp 7 = right plate of Capacitor 19 = left lead of Resistor 5. n10 = in+ of Op-Amp 1 = left plate of Capacitor 22, joined by the long steep diagonal that zigzags from the op-amp's lower pin at (371,171) up-left to (345,155), down-left to (326,187), up-left to (283,161) and then runs straight down to (183,330) before turning into the capacitor. n11 = in- of Op-Amp 4 = right plate of Capacitor 22 = left lead of Inductor 10. n12 = out of Op-Amp 4 = right lead of Inductor 10 = left lead of Resistor 8. Judgment calls: (a) the only 4-way crossing in the drawing is at (233,247), where that long n10 diagonal crosses the Op-Amp 12 output / Resistor 6 wire; an ASCII pixel dump shows the strokes stay 3-4 px through the intersection with no dot, so it is a crossover and n10 stays separate from n7; (b) Op-Amp 1 is the one stage whose in+ does NOT go to a ground -- it goes down to Capacitor 22 (n10); traced twice, the wire leaving the lower (+) pin is the zigzag, while the wire from Resistor 11 lands on the upper (-) pin 9 px higher up the triangle's left edge; (c) every ground symbol is a separate wire stub but all are named 0 per the rule; (d) 2-terminal components are indexed left-then-right as drawn along the tilted axis (top-then-bottom for the two sources), which affects no metric. No component was added, removed, re-classed or marked unconnected; nothing is off-frame.",
